<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Sul America to launch private pension plan.</title>
<headline>Brazil Sul America to launch private pension plan.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's largest insurer, Grupo Sul America, will expand its presence in the retail market by launching in the first week of October a private pension plan for individuals, a company official said.</p>
<p>Sul America hopes to have 30,000 clients by the end of 1997 with provisions totalling 20 million reais ($19.6 million), said Toni Lotar, director of Sul America Previdencia, the group's pension-business arm.</p>
</text>
